  - `Pattern` (Image Input, Square, Disc, Paraboloid, Bell, Gaussian, Thorn, Pyramid, Brick, Gradation, Waves, Half Bell, Ridged Bell, Crescent, Capsule, Cone): The tile shape, one of the built-in height profiles or Image Input for custom patterns. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern Specific` (0.0 to 1.0): Morphs the selected built-in shape (the effect depends on which pattern is chosen). (11 October 2026)
  - `Size Mode` (Normal / Interstice, Normal / Size, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel): How tile size is defined (the Normal modes by interstice or by size, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel). (11 October 2026)
  - `Interstice X/Y` (0.0 to 1.0): Gap between tiles, only in the interstice size mode. (11 October 2026)
  - `Scale` (0.0 to 2.0): Global scale of every tile. (11 October 2026)
  - `Scale Random` (0.0 to 1.0): Random scale variation per tile. (11 October 2026)
  - `Offset` (0.0 to 1.0): Incremental shift applied row after row (or column after column), which gives running-bond brick layouts. (11 October 2026)
  - `Position Random` (0.0 to 1.0): Random per-tile displacement, with separate X and Y control. (11 October 2026)
  - `Rotation [Rotation]` (0.0 to 1.0): Free rotation applied to all tiles. (11 October 2026)
  - `Rotation Random [Rotation]` (0.0 to 1.0): Random free rotation per tile. (11 October 2026)
  - `Luminance/Color Random` (0.0 to 1.0): Per-tile luminance variation, i.e. random tile heights in a height graph. (11 October 2026)
  - `Checker Mask` (False/True): Hides every other tile in a checkerboard fashion. (11 October 2026)
  - `Random Mask` (0.0 to 1.0): Randomly hides a proportion of tiles. (11 October 2026)
  - `Blending Mode` (Add, Max, Add Sub): How overlapping tiles combine (Add, Max, Add Sub). (11 October 2026)
