- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/blend (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: Combines a foreground and a background with a blending mode and an optional opacity mask; the most useful atomic node, comparable to two stacked layers with a blend mode in Photoshop or Painter. (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: Foreground (Grayscale/Color); Background (Grayscale/Color [primary]); Opacity (Grayscale) (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: (11 October 2026)
  - `Opacity` (Float): Opacity of the foreground, multiplied with the Opacity input. (11 October 2026)
  - `Blending mode` (Integer [static]): Blend operation: Copy, Add (linear dodge), Subtract, Multiply, Add Sub, Max (lighten), Min (darken), Switch, Divide, Overlay, Screen, Soft light. (11 October 2026)
  - `Alpha blending` (Integer [static]): How alpha is treated for colour inputs (use source alpha, ignore alpha, straight or premultiplied blending). (11 October 2026)
